<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      The next two came from electron-builder's template
      (app-builder-lib/templates/entitlements.mac.plist). Release builds are
      unsigned today, so electron-builder skips codesign and neither is applied;
      they only matter once a Developer ID identity is present.

      allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 needs only allow-jit (it maps code
      with MAP_JIT). @electron/osx-sign's own default.darwin.plist ships allow-jit
      without it. Remove it once a signed macOS build has been run through
      dictation (onnxruntime-node in a utilityProcess), a terminal (node-pty),
      code-index embedding and an agent-built tool with it absent.

      disable-library-validation: at pack time @electron/osx-sign walks all of
      Contents/ (Resources/app.asar.unpacked included) and signs every Mach-O
      file with the one identity, so the shipped .node/.dylib files (node-pty,
      onnxruntime-node, sharp/libvips under @huggingface/transformers) carry the
      app's team ID and would load with validation on. It stays because two
      loads are not ours to sign: an agent-built tool runs in a utilityProcess
      (it inherits this file) and may require a native addon from the user's
      workspace, and a .node left inside app.asar is extracted to a temp file
      by Electron before dlopen, unsigned. Remove it only after deciding that
      agent-built tools may not load workspace native addons, and with a test
      that every .node/.dylib in node_modules is matched by asarUnpack.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
